{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>But did not lie in wait.</b> Unintentionally. The sense of 'did not lie in wait' is that he did not act willfully in the matter, nor was he lying in wait to take his life; and Elohim brought it about under his hand, that he killed him because he had already incurred a death sentence for another offense — and therefore Scripture mentions Elohim, that is, by the attribute of justice. And this is what King Solomon, peace be upon him, said (Proverbs 13:23): ״ויש נספה בלא משפט״ — 'and some are swept away without justice' — that is, without justice for that offense, but on account of another offense for which he had already incurred liability." "<b>And already</b> our Rabbis of blessed memory brought a parable about this: two men, one killed willfully and one killed unintentionally, and the Holy One, blessed be He, arranged for them at a single inn. The one who killed unintentionally goes up a ladder and falls upon the one who killed willfully and kills him. The result: this one who killed willfully is killed, and that one who killed unintentionally goes into exile. And the reason it says ״מכה איש ומת״ — 'one who strikes a man and he dies' — is so that you not understand 'a man' to exclude a minor; therefore it was necessary to write elsewhere (Leviticus 24:17): ״ואיש כי יכה כל נפש אדם״ — 'and if a man strikes any living being of a person' — so that it be clarified from this, even minors. If so, why was 'a man' stated? To exclude the stillborn." "<b>And I will appoint for you a place.</b> That is, a designated place in the wilderness that would serve as a refuge for the unintentional killer, and this is the camp of Levi. And it appears to me that it is for this reason that Scripture mentioned the word 'for you' in this judgment, which it does not do in the other judgments — corresponding to Moses, who was of the tribe of Levi."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:02:27.601609469Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}